            <ArticleTitle>[A comparative study of the clinical effectiveness of Progestasert and Copper-T-200 (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>497-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In a comparative study Progestasert and Copper-T-200 were tested. Progestasert had a significantly higher expulsion rate and required removal due to bleeding, pain or medical reasons. As a consequence, 12 months after insertion the continuation rate of Progestasert was only 66.3% in comparison with 90.4% with Copper-T-200.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
